# The `(Model: v)` spelling of a nonprimitive formal rebound to an Other of another shape (two ints, no size_t `value`
# in its place): `v: o` is v's rebinding after o's admission to Model, exactly as for `(@: Model v)`
# (unit_ref_formal_rebind_other_refused), and the admission refuses it -- the method's implicit throw `implements`,
# uncaught, stops R0.  Were the store plain, the path through v would read the Other's cell (41) and the entry would
# be 7.  The positive sibling: unit_formal_spelling_rebind.
Model:
    size_t: value 1U
end: Model

Other:
    int: p 1
    int: q 2
end: Other

fn: m (Model: v) int
    o: merge: Other
    size_t: got 0U
    int: out 0
    o\p: 41
    v: o
    got: v\value
    if: got = 41U
        out: 7
    return: out
end: m

fn: check () int
    mo: merge: Model
return: m(mo)

sendMessage: exit(exit_code: check(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
